  "AICL is a protocol proposal — it does not guarantee that AI companies will pay.": "AICL mak proposta protokolu — ida ne'e la garante katak kompañia AI sira sei selu.",
  "AICL is the licensing and transaction layer built on top of AICR. Where AICR declares what is allowed, AICL defines how permission is actually obtained: license tiers and prices, quote and payment endpoints, signed license tokens, usage and audit logs, and revocation. It is designed to interoperate with emerging machine-payment mechanisms such as HTTP 402 flows and pay-per-crawl schemes, with agentic payment kept inside human-approved budgets and audit trails.": "AICL mak kamada lisensiamentu no transasaun ne'ebé harii iha leten AICR. Iha fatin ne'ebé AICR deklara saida mak permitidu, AICL define oinsá permisaun hetan realmente: nivel lisensa no presu, endpoint kotasaun no pagamentu, token lisensa ne'ebé asinadu, rejistru uzu no auditoria, no revogasaun. Ida ne'e dezeñu atu interopera ho mekanismu pagamentu-máquina ne'ebé foun hanesan fluxu HTTP 402 no eskema pay-per-crawl, ho pagamentu husi ajente mantein iha laran orsamentu ne'ebé ema aprova no rejistru auditoria.",
