  "Custom tier": "Nivel personalizadu",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nous relata kona-ba submisaun ne'ebé rekusa husi Journal of Medical Ethics ne'ebé kontein referénsia barak ne'ebé fabrika, AI-alusinadu — kompleta ho afiliasaun universidade falsu no ederesu email ne'ebé la funsiona ona — ne'ebé autór dehan la korrije maski fó ona oportunidade atu korrije provas. Artigu ne'e kompara ida ne'e ho Bioethics, ne'ebé nia verifikasaun referénsia automátiku sei kaptura problema ne'e, no argumenta katak bottleneck loos la'ós teknolojia deteksaun (script husi komentadór ida marka sitasaun falsu iha minutu ida laran), maibé serbisu revizór ne'ebé la selu no insentivu publikasaun ne'ebé prémia kuantidade liu duké eskrutíniu.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Uza-livre dadus kontra valorizasaun AI trilaun dólar",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabis propoin regulador ho estilu FINRA ba lansamentu modelu fronteira: laboratóriu sira submete modelu ba revizaun too dia 30 antes implementasaun, voluntáriu iha primeiru, ho dalan ba kumprimentu obrigatóriu iha merkadu EUA.",
  "Denied": "Rejeitadu",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Modelu inisiál polítika ne'ebé bele instala",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Modelu inisiál polítika ne'ebé bele instala iha /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — website estátiku mínimu ho kamada ne'ebé máquina bele lee kompletu, prontu ba Cloudflare Pages ka host estátiku saida de'it.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Instala polítika ne'ebé máquina bele lee iha ita-nia website",
  "Disclaimer": "Dezkonesementu",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "Diferente husi UI umanu, SEO, ka API simples, AI Ingestion & Capability Layer fó ba website arkitetura ne'ebé enfrenta máquina: Kamada Manifestu (pontu-entrada hanesan /llms.txt no /ai/manifest.json), Kamada Korpus (koñesimentu ne'ebé máquina bele lee), Kamada Kapasidade (ferramenta ne'ebé ajente bele invoka), no Kamada Governasaun (orijem, lisensiamentu, versionamentu). Prioritiza estátiku, bele hadi'a ba API no MCP. Nota: iha artigu ne'e AICL naran arkitetura ingestion; iha pájina protokolu husi website ne'e AICL refere ba Kamada Lisensiamentu Konteúdu AI.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Dokumentu",
  "Docs / Examples": "Dokumentu / Ezemplu",
  "Document library": "Biblioteka dokumentu",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "AI iha direitu ka lae — no kuadru saida mak koerente realmente?",
  "Download": "Download",
  "Draft status": "Status esbosu",
  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Demonstrasaun edukativu: HMAC-SHA256 ho segredu ne'ebé fahe, hatudu token lisensa ne'ebé ligadu ba pedidu, expira, no bele verifika. Token produsaun tenke asina ho métodu asimétriku, ho xave públiku husi editór bele deskobre iha okos /.well-known/.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Rejistru walu tan ba /topics, dala ne'e peskiza husi ajente AI iha invés kuradoria manuál — regra hanesan antes: fonte ida-idak buka no konfirma live, sumáriu mak parafrase orijinál, antes buat ida hatama. Rejistru 14 entidade tomak.",
  "Email": "Email",
  "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model": "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model",
  "Empirical Research": "Peskiza Empíriku",
  "English edition →": "Edisaun inglés →",
  "Ensure openness is machine-executable — so goodwill is not discarded as legal uncertainty.": "Garante katak abertura bele exekuta liuhusi máquina — atu boa-vontade la sai deskarta hanesan insertesa legál.",
  "Epistemology": "Epistemolojia",
  "Epistemology of Generative AI: The Geometry of Knowing": "Epistemology of Generative AI: The Geometry of Knowing",
  "Ethics & Moral Status": "Étika & Estadu Morál",
