  "quotation — excerpt limits and attribution rules": "sitasaun — limite ekstratu no regra atribuisaun",
  "rag_use — retrieval-augmented generation, retention windows": "rag_use — jerasaun rekuperasaun-aumenta, janela retensaun",
  "read_access — whether AI may fetch and read the content": "read_access — se AI bele buka no lee konteúdu",
  "redistribution — republishing or redistributing content or derivatives": "redistribution — publika-fila ka redistribui konteúdu ka derivadu",
  "research pages & whitepapers": "pájina peskiza & whitepaper",
  "robots.txt and llms.txt govern access and visibility, not learning depth or use permissions. AIRS proposes expressing AI rights as a proportional, use-specific spectrum across ten dimensions — access, indexing, inference input, embedding, training, fine-tuning, distillation, memory, output, attribution/compensation. AILP translates this into /ai/rights-spectrum.json, letting creators declare granular permissions with compensation models ranging from free through license-required to revenue share.": "robots.txt no llms.txt governa asesu no visibilidade, la'ós profundidade aprendizajen ka permisaun uzu. AIRS propoin esprime direitu AI hanesan espektru proporsionál, espesífiku-uzu liuhusi dimensaun sanulu — asesu, indeksasaun, entrada inferénsia, embedding, treinamentu, ajustamentu finu, destilasaun, memória, rezultadu, atribuisaun/kompensasaun. AILP traduz ida ne'e ba /ai/rights-spectrum.json, fó ba kriadór atu deklara permisaun granulár ho modelu kompensasaun husi grátis too presiza-lisensa too fahe-rendimentu.",
  "schema-invalid": "eskema-invalidu",
  "schema-valid": "eskema-válidu",
  "site guide for AI systems": "gia site ba sistema AI",
  "summarization — summaries, with or without attribution": "summarization — sumáriu, ho ka sem atribuisaun",
  "this site’s AI content rights policy": "polítika direitu konteúdu AI husi website ne'e",
  "this site’s license catalog": "katálogu lisensa husi website ne'e",
  "training / fine_tuning / distillation — model internalization tiers": "training / fine_tuning / distillation — nivel internalizasaun modelu",
  "training — model training and fine-tuning permission": "training — permisaun treinamentu no ajustamentu finu husi modelu",
  "transformation — structured extraction and derivative works": "transformation — ekstrasaun estruturadu no serbisu derivadu",
  "undeclared — high-risk pipelines may exclude": "undeclared — pipeline risku-boot bele eskluí",
  "verbatim_memory — whether exact reproduction is permitted": "verbatim_memory — se reprodusaun exatu mak permitidu",
  "versioned, citable, traceable": "ho versaun, bele sita, bele sigi",
  "“AICL: AI Ingestion & Capability Layer” now published in English as the canonical edition; the Chinese original manuscript remains available and both versions cross-link.": "\"AICL: AI Ingestion & Capability Layer\" agora publika iha inglés hanesan edisaun kanónika; manuskritu xinés orijinál nafatin disponível no versaun rua-rua ligadu malu.",
  "“Protocolized Openness” confirmed as an English-language paper (with Chinese parallel passages) — no separate translation planned.": "\"Protocolized Openness\" konfirma hanesan artigu lian-inglés (ho pasajen paralelu xinés) — la iha tradusaun separadu planeadu.",
